ll in the other room  because of a sound in a song that  sounded so different that I literally  thought something was happening far away  it is incredible now most reviewers have  said that the transparency mode it  sounds wonderful like it always has but  I've noticed some bigger differences I  think the biggest one is the accuracy of  the placement of transparent sound for  example you're walking outside instead  of hearing sounds and it sounds like  it's right there next to you you can  actually pinpoint that a car could be  driving from behind you on their right  hand side or on the left hand side that  is a major Improvement especially for  safety and the new adaptive transparency  mode has also been nice to have now I  tested this out and I was using my leaf  blower and I thought that it wasn't  really making much of a difference  holding it at arm's length and then when  I picked it up and brought it closer it  didn't get any louder because it was  limiting that sound and while I wouldn't  suggest this to be hearing protection  for you it is nice to have those super  loud annoying sounds brought down now as  far as usability the microphones have  also been improved with the originals I  would always ask people how do you hear  me and sometimes I'd have to switch over  to my phone I have not had a single  person complain about how I sounded  whether connected to my Mac or my iPhone  now as far as microphone quality the  original airpods which I'm using right  now they were never amazing they're okay  and lately they have also been  superseded and this is the microphone  quality of the airpods pro 2. now you  guys let me know in the comments if they  sound any better I've also started to  use the new sliding gesture on the  earbud to be able to adjust the volume I  had to force myself to do that to learn  and remember it and it has come in handy  I just wish they gave us a control to be  able to adjust how sensitive that is  because right now it barely makes a 